    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\nI implemented the audit logging in the owner-create endpoint (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, the handler for `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. Added an `org.slf4j.Logger` named `\"AUDIT\"` as a static field.\n2. After `saveOwner(...)` succeeds, it emits:\n   ```\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe log line is placed after the save so `owner.getId()` is populated, and it carries all three required values \u2014 owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`. The registration date renders in ISO form (`2026-08-17`), matching the JSON representation the test reads back. The acceptance test `coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
